        "min": 3,
        "titulo": "Pocket summary",
        "explicacao": "STEP 1: • 1. The Russian alphabet has 33 letters. But you only need to memorise about 15. The other 18 you already know or recognise. STEP 2: • 2. The letters fall into 4 groups: STEP 3: Identical to English (А, К, М, О, Т). STEP 4: False friends (В, Е, Н, Р, С, У, Х). STEP 5: New, but with familiar sounds (Б, Г, Д, Ё, З, И, Й, Л, П, Ф, Э, Ю, Я). STEP 6: Truly new, with new sounds (Ж, Ц, Ч, Ш, Щ, Ъ, Ы, Ь). STEP 7: • 3. The false friends are the biggest danger: STEP 8: В = V (not B) STEP 9: Е = YE (not E) STEP 10: Н = N (not H) STEP 11: Р = R (not P) STEP 12: С = S (not K) STEP 13: У = OO (not Y) STEP 14: Х = KH (not X) STEP 15: • 4. The Russian alphabet is phonetic. Each letter almost always has one fixed sound. This is a huge advantage. STEP 16: • 5. Two pronunciation rules to learn now: STEP 17: Unstressed О becomes А: окно́ = ahk-NOH, молоко́ = mah-lah-KOH. STEP 18: Voiced consonants at the end become voiceless: друг = drook, хлеб = khlyep. STEP 19: • 6. Hard and soft vowels: STEP 20: Hard: А, О, У, Э, Ы STEP 21: Soft: Я, Ё, Ю, Е, И STEP 22: • 7. The big insight: the Russian alphabet is much friendlier than it looks. You have already read six Russian signs in this lesson. In one hour, you will be able to read any sign.",
